# Project
Spanish-language mobility analytics app on MiBici open data (Guadalajara). Built solo in short sprints.
The demo must run locally with no internet and no model. Anything that risks that is out of scope.

# Architecture
- `src/ingestion.py` loads and cleans. Do not change its column names: trips have start, end, origin_id, dest_id, minutes, hour, weekday, date.
- `src/analytics.py` and `src/imbalance.py` are pure functions on DataFrames. No Streamlit, no LLM, no file access inside them.
- `src/copilot.py` answers only by calling those functions as tools.
- `src/llm.py` is the only place that talks to a model. Use `llm.chat()`. If it returns None, show the deterministic answer.
- `app.py` is layout only. No calculations in it.

# Data integrity
- Never fabricate, estimate or hard-code a statistic. Every number on screen traces to a function in src.
- Never drop rows silently. Use the CleanReport.
- Flows are historical. Never state or imply how many bikes are at a station now.
- Sample data under data/sample is synthetic. Label it on screen whenever it is in use.

# Working style
- Make `tests/test_analytics_spec.py` pass one function at a time. Do not edit the tests.
- Run `pytest -q` after every change and fix failures before moving on.
- Small functions, type hints, no new dependencies beyond requirements.txt.
- UI text and model answers in Spanish. Code, comments and commit messages in English.
- Commit after each passing step.

# Out of scope
Real-time APIs, authentication, databases, Docker, multi-agent setups, forecasting models, maps before everything else works.
